 and not the implementation): 617 calls resolved alike, 0 to different targets. Downstream: `effects` purity of the algebra basis 32 → 34 pure (`positions`, `spans`), and loopcost's own lexical fallback for calls was removed (it keeps the rule for a function passed BY NAME). `tests/lexicalscope_spec.lua`. CART-1059 |"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},"id":"1791227034.508396-edit","verb":"edit"}],"version":1,"explained":11227,"entries":[{"decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"args":{"file":"lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua","before":"local function resolve_local_callable(cv, node_index, exact, addref, parent_fn)","after":"-- LEXICAL SCOPE for a same-file refusal (CART-1485): a name defined several times in ONE file — core.lua's many nested\n-- `local function walk` — is one binding at each call. A definition is VISIBLE from the call when the function\n-- enclosing it (parent_fn; none = file level) is on the call's enclosing chain; the INNERMOST visible one wins, and\n-- within one scope the latest declared before the call (a re-declaration shadows the earlier one). A forward-declared\n-- `local f; … function f(…)` is a definition in that scope like any other. -> the node, or nil (still ambiguous).\n-- Lua's scoping, asked only for Lua files; the acceptance joined it against the algebra's lua_scope_graph over lua/:\n-- 617 calls resolved alike, 0 to different targets.\nlocal function lexical_pick(cands, file, fn, call_at, parent_fn)\n    if not (fn and call_at and file:match('%.lua$')) then return nil end\n    local depth, d, f = {}, 0, fn\n    while f do depth[f.id] = d; d = d + 1; f = parent_fn[f.id] end\n    local cl, cc = atr.sl(call_at), atr.sc(call_at)\n    local best, bdepth, bl, bc, tie\n    for _, n in ipairs(cands or {}) do\n        if n.file == file and not n.cbarg and n.range then\n            local p = parent_fn[n.id]\n            local nd = p == nil and d or depth[p.id]\n            if nd then\n                local l, c = atr.sl(n.range), atr.sc(n.range)\n                local before = l < cl or (l == cl and c <= cc)\n                if not best or nd < bdepth then best, bdepth, bl, bc, tie = n, nd, l, c, not before\n                elseif nd == bdepth then\n                    -- (one scope, two declarations: the latest one declared before the call)\n                    local bbefore = bl < cl or (bl == cl and bc <= cc)\n                    if before and (not bbefore or l > bl or (l == bl and c > bc)) then best, bl, bc, tie = n, l, c, false\n                    elseif not bbefore and not before then tie = true end\n                end\n            end\n        end\n    end\n    if tie then return nil end\n    return best\nend\nM._lexical_pick = lexical_pick\n\nlocal function resolve_local_callable(cv, node_index, exact, addref, parent_fn)"},"touched":["lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua"],"verb":"edit"},"id":"1791226310.689038-edit","bytes":1737,"decided_by":"tactic"},{"decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"args":{"file":"lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua","before":"            if not shadowed and not fdef then\n                target, inferred, refused, ext = resolve(p.full or p.call.callee, p.file)\n            end","after":"            if not shadowed and not fdef then\n                target, inferred, refused, ext = resolve(p.full or p.call.callee, p.file)\n                if refused and refused.rule == 'samefile' then\n                    local pick = lexical_pick(refused.cands, p.file, from and node_index[from], p.at, parent_fn)\n                    if pick then target, inferred, refused = pick, false, nil end\n                end\n            end"},"touched":["lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua"],"verb":"edit"},"id":"1791226311.068956-edit","bytes":165,"decided_by":"tactic"},{"decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"args":{"file":"lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua","before":"                target, inferred, refused, ext = resolve(cfull or ccallee, cfile)\n            end\n            if target t","after":"                target, inferred, refused, ext = resolve(cfull or ccallee, cfile)\n                if refused and refused.rule == 'samefile' and not cfull then\n                    local pick = M._lexical_pick(refused.cands, cfile, cfn and node_index[cfn], cget(i, 'at'), parent_fn) -- (via M: this function is at the 60-upvalue limit)\n                    if pick then target, inferred, refused = pick, false, nil end\n                end\n            end\n            if target t"},"touched":["lua/cartograph/providers/treesitter.lua"],"verb":"edit"},"id":"1791226362.802765-edit","bytes":179,"decided_by":"tactic"},{"decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"args":{"file":"tests/lexicalscope_spec.lua","before":"","after":"-- LEXICAL SCOPE for a same-file name (CART-1485): a name defined several times in one Lua file — nested `local\n-- function walk` in many functions, as core.lua writes them — was refused `samefile` at every call. Each call has ONE\n-- binding: the innermost definition whose enclosing function is on the call's chain, the latest one declared before\n-- the call within a scope. Pinned: the recursive call and the outer call of two nested walks, a re-declaration, a\n-- forward-declared local, and a name that is genuinely two file-level definitions (still refused).\n\nlocal ts = require 'cartograph.providers.treesitter'\n\nlocal SRC = table.concat({\n    'local M = {}',\n    'function M.a(t)',\n    '  local function walk(x) if x > 0 then return walk(x - 1) end return 0 end',\n    '  return walk(t)',\n    'end',\n    'function M.b(t)',\n    '  local function walk(x) return x end',\n    '  return walk(t)',\n    'end',\n    'function M.c(t)',\n    '  local function pick(x) return 1 end',\n    '  local function pick(x) return 2 end',\n    '  return pick(t)',\n    'end',\n    'local build',\n    'local function g() return build(1) end',\n    'function build(x) return x end',\n    'local function twice() return 1 end',\n    'local function twice() return 2 end',\n    'local function h() return twice() end',\n    'return M', '' }, '\\n')\n\nlocal function calls_of(data, callee)\n    local out = {}\n    for _, c in ipairs(data.calls) do\n        if c.callee == callee then out[#out + 1] = { line = c.line or (require('cartograph.at').sl(c.at) + 1), to = c.to, refused = c.refused and c.refused.rule } end\n    end\n    table.sort(out, function (x, y) return x.line < y.line end)\n    return out\nend\n\nlocal function line_of(data, id)\n    for _, n in ipairs(data.nodes) do if n.id == id then return require('cartograph.at').sl(n.range) + 1 end end\nend\n\ntest('lexical scope: a nested local function\\'s calls — its own recursion and its parent\\'s — reach THAT definition, a re-declaration the later one; two file-level definitions stay refused (CART-1485)', function ()\n    if not parser_available('lua') then skip 'no lua parser' end\n    local root = vim.fn.tempname(); vim.fn.mkdir(root, 'p')\n    local fd = assert(io.open(root .. '/m.lua', 'w')); fd:write(SRC); fd:close()\n    local data = ts.extract(root)\n    vim.fn.delete(root, 'rf')\n    local walks = calls_of(data, 'walk')\n    eq(3, #walks)\n    eq(3, line_of(data, walks[1].to), 'a\\'s walk calling itself')\n    eq(3, line_of(data, walks[2].to), 'a calling its walk')\n    eq(7, line_of(data, walks[3].to), 'b calling ITS walk')\n    eq(12, line_of(data, calls_of(data, 'pick')[1].to), 'the later of two declarations in one scope')\n    eq(17, line_of(data, calls_of(data, 'build')[1].to), 'the forward-declared local')\n    local tw = calls_of(data, 'twice')[1]\n    eq(nil, tw.to); eq('samefile', tw.refused, 'two file-level definitions before the call: the later shadows — but both are file level, and')\nend)"},"touched":["tests/lexicalscope_spec.lua"],"verb":"edit"},"id":"1791226390.822564-edit","bytes":2314,"decided_by":"tactic"},{"decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"args":{"file":"